IMPORT prelude

-- National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009 (Cth) -- the licence requirement and what follows from breaking it (ss 6
-- item 1, 29, 32, 180), the responsible lending duties of a licensee that is a credit provider (Part 3-2 Divisions 3 and 4:
-- ss 128-133, with s 160F), credit limit increase invitations on credit cards (ss 133BA, 133BE), small amount and short-term
-- credit contracts (s 5 definitions, s 133CA), and in the National Credit Code (Schedule 1): when the Code applies (ss 4, 5),
-- mortgages (ss 7, 42, 43), and the caps on what a small amount credit contract may charge (ss 23A, 31A, 31B, 31C, 39B).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 52, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 57, 2026), register id
-- C2026C00340, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2009A00134.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0017 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1), raised 5 times by the Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave scenarios: Chloe c043 (2024-06-10, a credit card at 21: what must a lender assess?), c052
-- (2028-05-15, settlement and the mortgage: the National Credit Code); Jake k048 (2031-03-02, two credit cards at 24: ss
-- 128-133, 133BE), k049 (2032-08-20, a $2,000 small-amount loan: "s 31A ... 20% establishment fee, 4% a month", s 31B --
-- what is the most a payday lender may charge, and what if it charges more?), k063 (2036-08-22, a friend's debt to an
-- unlicensed lender: s 29 -- is the loan enforceable?). SCOPED to those provisions and questions, with the definitions,
-- conditions and exceptions needed to answer them. The ss 31A and 31B the scenario names are sections of the National Credit
-- Code in Schedule 1, not of the Act itself; they are encoded as such.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The licensing regime itself (Part 2-2), credit assistance (Part 3-1), standard home loans (Part 3-2A), Key Facts
-- Sheets (ss 133BB-133BD), the rest of Part 3-2C, comprehensive credit reporting (Part 3-2CA), hardship and enforcement under
-- the Code, the Code's other exclusions (s 6), disclosure, interest and the unjust transactions provisions. Everything the
-- regulations or ASIC may prescribe -- a different assessment period (s 128), prescribed inquiries (s 130(1)(d), (e)),
-- prescribed unsuitability circumstances (ss 131(2)(c), 133(2)(c)) and situations taken not to be unsuitable (s 133(5)), the
-- ASIC period under s 160F for credit cards, a different $2,000 ceiling or 1-year term for small amount credit contracts,
-- fees prescribed under s 31B(2)(b) -- are INPUTS. The dollar value of a penalty unit is not in this Act and is not encoded.
-- Whether a contract is a continuing or low cost credit contract (Code ss 204, 13E) is an INPUT.
--
-- DATES are written as numbers YYYYMMDD, so the n-th anniversary of a day D is D + n x 10000. "Within 2 years of" a day is
-- read as before its second anniversary; the period that "ends 7 years after" a day as including the seventh anniversary.
-- This is the encoder's convention, not the Act's. A year is taken as 365 days for the small amount credit contract term.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive encodings (the
-- writing-l4-rules skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no
-- human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009 -- licensing, responsible lending, small amount credit`

§§ `ss 6 item 1, 29, 32 -- credit activities without a licence`

-- s 6(1) item 1: a person engages in a credit activity if "(a) the person is a credit provider under a credit contract; or
-- (b) the person carries on a business of providing credit, being credit the provision of which the National Credit Code
-- applies to; or (c) the person performs the obligations, or exercises the rights, of a credit provider in relation to a
-- credit contract or proposed credit contract (whether the person does so as the credit provider or on behalf of the credit
-- provider)". (Items 2-5 -- credit services, consumer leases, mortgages, guarantees -- are not encoded.)
-- s 29(1): "A person must not engage in a credit activity if the person does not hold a licence authorising the person to
-- engage in the credit activity." Civil penalty: 5,000 penalty units. (2): offence, 2 years imprisonment.
-- (3): a defence if the person acts "on behalf of another person (the principal)", is an "employee or director" of the
-- principal (or of a related body corporate) or a "credit representative" of the principal, acts "within the authority of the
-- principal", and "the principal holds a licence". (4): the same for a representative of a principal exempted under s 109 or
-- s 110.
-- s 32(1): a person must not "demand, receive or accept any fee, charge or other amount from a consumer for engaging in a
-- credit activity" if by engaging in it the person contravenes s 29. Civil penalty 5,000 penalty units; offence 1 year.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `is a credit provider under a credit contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries on a business of providing credit to which the Code applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exercises the rights of a credit provider, for itself or on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a licence authorising the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts within authority as employee, director or credit representative of a licensed principal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts within authority as representative of a principal exempted under s 109 or s 110` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `engages in a credit activity` IF
        `the person`'s `is a credit provider under a credit contract`
    OR  `the person`'s `carries on a business of providing credit to which the Code applies`
    OR  `the person`'s `exercises the rights of a credit provider, for itself or on its behalf`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contravenes s 29` IF
        `engages in a credit activity` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a licence authorising the activity`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `acts within authority as employee, director or credit representative of a licensed principal`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `acts within authority as representative of a principal exempted under s 109 or s 110`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 32 forbids it to take any fee from the consumer` IF
    `contravenes s 29` `the person`

§§ `s 180 -- orders in relation to unlawful credit activities`

-- s 180(1): if "(a) a person (the defendant) engages in a credit activity in relation to another person (the plaintiff); and
-- (b) the engaging in the activity contravenes ... (i) section 29 ...; (ii) section 124A ...; (iii) section 133CA", the court
-- "may make such order as the court considers appropriate". (2) examples: "(a) an order declaring the whole or any part of a
-- contract ... to be void"; "(c) an order refusing to enforce any or all of the terms of such a contract"; "(d) an order
-- directing the defendant to refund money". (3): "only if: (a) the plaintiff or ASIC (on behalf of the plaintiff) applies ...;
-- and (b) the application is made within 6 years of the day the cause of action ... accrued". (4): ASIC only "if the
-- plaintiff has given consent in writing before the application is made".
-- The Act does not make an unlicensed lender's contract void or unenforceable of itself: the court MAY, on an application by
-- the person the credit activity was engaged in relation to (or ASIC with that person's written consent), in time.
DECLARE `Application for orders` HAS
    `the defendant engaged in a credit activity in relation to the applicant's side` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the activity contravened s 29, s 124A or s 133CA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made by the plaintiff` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made by ASIC with the plaintiff's prior written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cause of action accrued on` IS A NUMBER
    `made on` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application for orders`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order under s 180, including refusing to enforce the contract` IF
        `the application`'s `the defendant engaged in a credit activity in relation to the applicant's side`
    AND `the application`'s `the activity contravened s 29, s 124A or s 133CA`
    AND (`the application`'s `made by the plaintiff` OR `the application`'s `made by ASIC with the plaintiff's prior written consent`)
    AND `the application`'s `made on` LESS THAN `the application`'s `cause of action accrued on` PLUS 60000

§§ `Code ss 4, 5 -- credit to which the National Credit Code applies`

-- Code s 4: "a credit contract is a contract under which credit is or may be provided, being the provision of credit to which
-- this Code applies". s 5(1): the Code applies if, when the contract is entered into, "(a) the debtor is a natural person or a
-- strata corporation; and (b) the credit is provided or intended to be provided wholly or predominantly: (i) for personal,
-- domestic or household purposes; or (ii) to purchase, renovate or improve residential property for investment purposes; or
-- (iii) to refinance" such investment credit; "(c) a charge is or may be made for providing the credit; and (d) the credit
-- provider provides the credit in the course of a business of providing credit carried on in this jurisdiction or as part of
-- or incidentally to any other business". (3): "investment by the debtor is not a personal, domestic or household purpose".
-- (4): the predominant purpose is "the purpose for which more than half of the credit is intended to be used".
-- The exclusions in s 6 (short term credit, pawnbrokers, employee loans and so on) are not encoded.
DECLARE Credit HAS
    `the debtor is a natural person or strata corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount of credit` IS A NUMBER
    `amount for personal, domestic or household purposes or residential investment property` IS A NUMBER
    `a charge is or may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provided in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the credit` IS A Credit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the National Credit Code applies` IF
        `the credit`'s `the debtor is a natural person or strata corporation`
    AND `the credit`'s `amount for personal, domestic or household purposes or residential investment property` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `the credit`'s `amount of credit`
    AND `the credit`'s `a charge is or may be made`
    AND `the credit`'s `provided in the course of a business`

§§ `Code ss 7, 42, 43 -- the home loan mortgage`

-- Code s 7(1): the Code applies to a mortgage if "(a) it secures obligations under a credit contract or a related guarantee;
-- and (b) the mortgagor is a natural person or a strata corporation".
-- s 42(1): "A mortgage must be in the form of a written mortgage document that is signed by the mortgagor." (2): it is enough
-- if it is "contained in a credit contract signed by the mortgagor" or one of the documents is signed and refers to the
-- others. (4): "A mortgage is not enforceable unless it complies with this section." ((3), goods mortgages, not encoded.)
-- s 43(1): a written mortgage that is not part of the credit contract -- the credit provider must give the mortgagor a copy
-- "within 14 days after it is made" (unless already given, (2)).
-- Registration of the mortgage on the title is a matter for the Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA), not this Act.
DECLARE Mortgage HAS
    `secures obligations under a credit contract or related guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the mortgagor is a natural person or strata corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in a written document signed by the mortgagor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in a credit contract signed by the mortgagor` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A Mortgage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Code applies to the mortgage` IF
        `the mortgage`'s `secures obligations under a credit contract or related guarantee`
    AND `the mortgage`'s `the mortgagor is a natural person or strata corporation`

GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A Mortgage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Code makes the mortgage unenforceable` IF
        `the Code applies to the mortgage` `the mortgage`
    AND (NOT `the mortgage`'s `is in a written document signed by the mortgagor`)
    AND (NOT `the mortgage`'s `is in a credit contract signed by the mortgagor`)

GIVEN `the mortgage` IS A Mortgage
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days the credit provider has to give the mortgagor a copy` MEANS
    IF `the Code applies to the mortgage` `the mortgage`
       AND `the mortgage`'s `is in a written document signed by the mortgagor`
       AND (NOT `the mortgage`'s `is in a credit contract signed by the mortgagor`)
    THEN 14
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 128-133, 160F -- the obligation to assess unsuitability, and the prohibition on unsuitable contracts`

-- s 128: a licensee must not "(a) enter a credit contract with a consumer who will be the debtor", or "(b) increase the credit
-- limit", or make an unconditional representation of eligibility or of an increase ((aa), (ba)), on a day (the credit day)
-- "unless the licensee has, within 90 days (or other period prescribed by the regulations ...) before the credit day: (c) made
-- an assessment that: (i) is in accordance with section 129; and (ii) covers the period in which the credit day occurs; and (d)
-- made the inquiries and verification in accordance with section 130." Civil penalty: 5,000 penalty units.
-- s 129: the assessment "(a) specifies the period the assessment covers; and (b) assesses whether the credit contract will be
-- unsuitable for the consumer".
-- s 130(1): before the assessment, "(a) make reasonable inquiries about the consumer's requirements and objectives ...; (b) make
-- reasonable inquiries about the consumer's financial situation; and (c) take reasonable steps to verify the consumer's
-- financial situation" and the prescribed inquiries and steps ((d), (e)). (1A): for a small amount credit contract, where the
-- consumer holds an ADI account into which income is credited, "obtain and consider information about each transaction on the
-- account, and the balances of the account, during at least the immediately preceding period of 90 days".
DECLARE Assessment HAS
    `days before the credit day it was made` IS A NUMBER
    `the period prescribed instead of 90 days` IS A NUMBER
    `specifies the period it covers and covers the credit day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inquired into requirements and objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inquired into the financial situation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took reasonable steps to verify the financial situation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made the prescribed inquiries and steps` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is for a small amount credit contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consumer has an ADI account into which income is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of that account's transactions and balances considered` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the assessment` IS AN Assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 130 inquiries and verification were made` IF
        `the assessment`'s `inquired into requirements and objectives`
    AND `the assessment`'s `inquired into the financial situation`
    AND `the assessment`'s `took reasonable steps to verify the financial situation`
    AND `the assessment`'s `made the prescribed inquiries and steps`
    AND (    (NOT `the assessment`'s `is for a small amount credit contract`)
         OR  (NOT `the assessment`'s `the consumer has an ADI account into which income is paid`)
         OR  `the assessment`'s `days of that account's transactions and balances considered` AT LEAST 90)

GIVEN `the assessment` IS AN Assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 128 is satisfied` IF
        `the assessment`'s `days before the credit day it was made` AT LEAST 0
    AND `the assessment`'s `days before the credit day it was made` AT MOST `the assessment`'s `the period prescribed instead of 90 days`
    AND `the assessment`'s `specifies the period it covers and covers the credit day`
    AND `the s 130 inquiries and verification were made` `the assessment`

-- s 131(2) (at the time of the assessment) and s 133(2) (at the time the contract is entered or the limit increased): the
-- contract is unsuitable if "(a) [it is likely that] the consumer will be unable to comply with the consumer's financial
-- obligations under the contract, or could only comply with substantial hardship; or (b) the contract will not meet [does not
-- meet] the consumer's requirements or objectives; or (c)" prescribed circumstances apply.
-- (3): "if the consumer could only comply ... by selling the consumer's principal place of residence, the consumer could only
-- comply with those obligations with substantial hardship, unless the contrary is proved."
-- (3AA): substantial hardship is taken if "(a) the contract is a credit card contract; and (b) the consumer could not comply
-- with an obligation to repay an amount equal to the credit limit of the contract within the period determined by ASIC under
-- section 160F". The ASIC period is a legislative instrument, not deposited: what the consumer could repay within it is an
-- INPUT.
-- s 131(1): the licensee "must assess that the credit contract will be unsuitable" when (2) says so. Civil penalty.
-- s 133(1): a licensee must not enter the contract or increase the limit "if the contract is unsuitable for the consumer under
-- subsection (2)". Civil penalty 5,000 penalty units; offence 2 years. (5): regulations may prescribe situations in which a
-- contract "is taken not to be unsuitable".
-- s 133BA(1): "A credit card contract is a continuing credit contract under which credit is ordinarily obtained only by the use
-- of a credit card."
-- Naive simplification: the facts at the assessment and at entry are taken to be the same, so one record serves both.
DECLARE `Consumer position` HAS
    `likely unable to comply with the obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `could comply only with substantial hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `could comply only by selling the principal place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contrary of hardship is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a credit card contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `credit limit` IS A NUMBER
    `amount the consumer could repay within the ASIC period` IS A NUMBER
    `meets the consumer's requirements and objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a prescribed unsuitability circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a regulation takes it not to be unsuitable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the position` IS A `Consumer position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer could comply only with substantial hardship` IF
        `the position`'s `could comply only with substantial hardship`
    OR  (`the position`'s `could comply only by selling the principal place of residence` AND (NOT `the position`'s `the contrary of hardship is proved`))
    OR  (`the position`'s `is a credit card contract` AND `the position`'s `amount the consumer could repay within the ASIC period` LESS THAN `the position`'s `credit limit`)

GIVEN `the position` IS A `Consumer position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is unsuitable under s 131(2) and s 133(2)` IF
        `the position`'s `likely unable to comply with the obligations`
    OR  `the consumer could comply only with substantial hardship` `the position`
    OR  (NOT `the position`'s `meets the consumer's requirements and objectives`)
    OR  `the position`'s `a prescribed unsuitability circumstance applies`

GIVEN `the position` IS A `Consumer position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 133 forbids entering the contract or increasing the limit` IF
        `the contract is unsuitable under s 131(2) and s 133(2)` `the position`
    AND (NOT `the position`'s `a regulation takes it not to be unsuitable`)

GIVEN `the assessment` IS AN Assessment, `the position` IS A `Consumer position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee may enter the contract` IF
        `s 128 is satisfied` `the assessment`
    AND (NOT `s 133 forbids entering the contract or increasing the limit` `the position`)

-- s 132(2): if, in the period that starts on the credit day and "ends 7 years after that day", the consumer asks for a copy of
-- the assessment, the licensee must give a written copy "(c) if the request is made within 2 years of the credit day--before
-- the end of 7 business days after the day the licensee receives the request; and (d) otherwise--before the end of 21
-- business days". (4): the licensee "must not request or demand payment". (1): a request before entry -- before entering.
-- Returns the business days allowed, or 0 where s 132(2) imposes no duty.
GIVEN `credit day` IS A NUMBER, `request received on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`business days to give a copy of the assessment` MEANS
    IF `request received on` LESS THAN `credit day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `request received on` LESS THAN `credit day` PLUS 20000
         THEN 7
         ELSE IF `request received on` AT MOST `credit day` PLUS 70000
              THEN 21
              ELSE 0

§§ `s 133BE -- credit limit increase invitations`

-- s 133BE(1): "A licensee who is the credit provider under a credit card contract must not make a credit limit increase
-- invitation in relation to the contract." Civil penalty 5,000 penalty units; offence 100 penalty units; strict liability 20.
-- (5): it makes one if it gives the debtor "any form of communication that relates to the contract" and "(i) the
-- communication offers to increase the credit limit ...; (ii) ... invites the consumer to apply for an increase ...; (iii) the
-- licensee gave the communication ... for the purpose (or for purposes including the purpose) of encouraging the consumer to
-- consider applying for an increase". Regulations may say more ((6), not encoded).
-- s 133BE is not an assessment provision: the credit limit assessment is s 131(3AA) and s 133(3AA) above.
DECLARE Communication HAS
    `from the credit provider under a credit card contract to the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `offers to increase the credit limit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `invites an application for an increase` IS A BOOLEAN
    `given for a purpose including encouraging an application for an increase` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the communication` IS A Communication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 133BE forbids the communication` IF
        `the communication`'s `from the credit provider under a credit card contract to the debtor`
    AND (    `the communication`'s `offers to increase the credit limit`
         OR  `the communication`'s `invites an application for an increase`
         OR  `the communication`'s `given for a purpose including encouraging an application for an increase`)

§§ `s 5 definitions, s 133CA -- small amount and short-term credit contracts`

-- s 5: "small amount credit contract: a credit contract is a small amount credit contract if: (a) the contract is not a
-- continuing credit contract or a low cost credit contract; and (b) the credit provider under the contract is not an ADI; and
-- (c) the credit limit of the contract is $2,000 (or such other amount as is prescribed by the regulations) or less; and (d)
-- the term of the contract is at least 16 days but not longer than 1 year (or such other number of years as is prescribed by
-- the regulations); and (e) the debtor's obligations under the contract are not, and will not be, secured; and (f) the
-- contract meets any other requirements prescribed by the regulations."
-- "short-term credit contract": (a)-(c) the same, "(d) the term of the contract is 15 days or less; and (e) the contract meets
-- any other requirements prescribed by the regulations" -- secured or not.
-- s 133CA(1): a licensee must not enter, or increase the credit limit of, a short-term credit contract. Civil penalty 5,000
-- penalty units; offence 50 penalty units.
DECLARE Loan HAS
    `is a continuing or low cost credit contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the credit provider is an ADI` IS A BOOLEAN
    `credit limit` IS A NUMBER
    `the prescribed credit limit ceiling` IS A NUMBER
    `term in days` IS A NUMBER
    `the prescribed maximum term in years` IS A NUMBER
    `is secured` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets any other prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `adjusted credit amount` IS A NUMBER
    `refinances credit under another small amount credit contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `establishment fee` IS A NUMBER
    `monthly fee` IS A NUMBER
    `interest charged` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a small amount credit contract` IF
        (NOT `the loan`'s `is a continuing or low cost credit contract`)
    AND (NOT `the loan`'s `the credit provider is an ADI`)
    AND `the loan`'s `credit limit` AT MOST `the loan`'s `the prescribed credit limit ceiling`
    AND `the loan`'s `term in days` AT LEAST 16
    AND `the loan`'s `term in days` AT MOST `the loan`'s `the prescribed maximum term in years` TIMES 365
    AND (NOT `the loan`'s `is secured`)
    AND `the loan`'s `meets any other prescribed requirements`

GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a short-term credit contract` IF
        (NOT `the loan`'s `is a continuing or low cost credit contract`)
    AND (NOT `the loan`'s `the credit provider is an ADI`)
    AND `the loan`'s `credit limit` AT MOST `the loan`'s `the prescribed credit limit ceiling`
    AND `the loan`'s `term in days` AT MOST 15
    AND `the loan`'s `meets any other prescribed requirements`

GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 133CA forbids a licensee to enter it` IF
    `is a short-term credit contract` `the loan`

§§ `Code ss 23A, 31A, 31B, 31C, 39B -- what a small amount credit contract may charge`

-- Code s 31A(1): a small amount credit contract "must not impose or provide for fees and charges" other than "(a) a permitted
-- establishment fee; (b) a fee or charge (a permitted monthly fee) that is payable on a monthly basis starting on the day the
-- contract is entered into; (c) a fee or charge that is payable in the event of a default in payment ...; (d) a government
-- fee, charge or duty". (1A): no permitted establishment fee "if any of the amount of credit ... is to refinance any of the
-- amount of credit provided to the debtor under another small amount credit contract". (2): "A permitted establishment fee is
-- a fee or charge the amount of which must not exceed 20% of the adjusted credit amount". (3): a permitted monthly fee "must
-- not exceed 4% of the adjusted credit amount".
-- Code Schedule dictionary: "adjusted credit amount, in relation to a small amount credit contract, means the first amount of
-- credit that is, or is to be, provided under the contract."
-- s 23A(1): a small amount credit contract "must not impose a monetary liability on the debtor: (a) in respect of an interest
-- charge (including a default rate of interest)"; nor a prohibited fee, nor more than the Code allows. (2): the provisions
-- imposing it are void and the debtor "may recover as a debt due to the debtor any amount paid".
-- s 31B(1): a credit provider "must not require or accept payment by the debtor of a fee or charge" in relation to a small
-- amount credit contract unless (2) it "may be imposed ... under section 31A" or is prescribed. Criminal penalty 100 penalty
-- units. (3): "the debtor is not liable (and is taken never to have been liable) to make the payment" and "may recover as a
-- debt due to the debtor the amount of any payment made".
-- READING (the encoder's, labelled): a fee above the cap is not "a permitted establishment fee" (or monthly fee) at all, so
-- under s 31B(3) the debtor is not liable for ANY of it, not merely the excess. The text is consistent with that reading; it
-- does not say "to the extent of the excess".
-- s 31C: no "unexpired monthly fee" -- a monthly fee for a month that commences after the contract is paid out.
-- s 39B(1): after a default, the credit provider must not "recover more than twice the adjusted credit amount" (whether by
-- repayments or otherwise); (3) enforcement expenses are outside the cap.
GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest permitted establishment fee` MEANS
    IF `the loan`'s `refinances credit under another small amount credit contract`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the loan`'s `adjusted credit amount` TIMES 20 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the largest permitted monthly fee` MEANS
    `the loan`'s `adjusted credit amount` TIMES 4 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the permitted establishment and monthly fees can come to` MEANS
    `the largest permitted establishment fee` `the loan` PLUS `the largest permitted monthly fee` `the loan` TIMES `months`

GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the charges comply with ss 23A and 31A` IF
        `the loan`'s `establishment fee` AT MOST `the largest permitted establishment fee` `the loan`
    AND `the loan`'s `monthly fee` AT MOST `the largest permitted monthly fee` `the loan`
    AND `the loan`'s `interest charged` EQUALS 0

-- What the debtor is not liable for, per instalment structure: the establishment fee if over its cap, each monthly fee if over
-- its cap (counted once here), and any interest (s 23A).
GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount the debtor is not liable to pay` MEANS
        (IF `the loan`'s `establishment fee` GREATER THAN `the largest permitted establishment fee` `the loan`
         THEN `the loan`'s `establishment fee` ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `the loan`'s `monthly fee` GREATER THAN `the largest permitted monthly fee` `the loan`
          THEN `the loan`'s `monthly fee` ELSE 0)
    PLUS `the loan`'s `interest charged`

GIVEN `the loan` IS A Loan
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most recoverable after a default, before enforcement expenses` MEANS
    `the loan`'s `adjusted credit amount` TIMES 2

GIVEN `month starts on` IS A NUMBER, `paid out on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the monthly fee for that month is an unexpired monthly fee` IF
    `month starts on` GREATER THAN `paid out on`
